# Fixed defect 131's class, 2026-10-01, ruling 5 of the recovery batches (lane
# recovery-b5's C1), the shapes beside the habit. Where a run maps onto its
# levels by a guess, its fix is a guess: a body in tabs at its head's own
# margin, read one level under the head since a tab's width is the editor's;
# a margin of a tab and spaces; a jump read through the habit, laid out one
# level deeper and told by the run's one message, never as
# `indentation_jump`. Where the two-space reading would put a line one level
# under a line that opens nothing, it is read as a four-space line, out of
# the run, and told as it always was: a slip at six over a correct line at
# eight is the slip's message alone, a slip at seven beside one at six is its
# own, two spaces over a statement stay an over-indent. Three spaces a level
# are no run, a message a line as before. A line in a run still tells its own
# mistake: a stray `)`, a tab between words, a line left open. `check
# --apply` writes the certain fixes and leaves the guesses (`.applied`).

